From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:53:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pin the swig build dependency to 4.3.1 for riscv64

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 build portability]

pyproject.toml pins swig>=4.4.0 only because that is the version upstream
happened to be on when it replaced the removed $function exception
variable with $action (SWIG CHANGES, 2025-06-09: "$action (added in
2001) ... has exactly the same value"). $action has worked since SWIG
2001, so the project's own .i files (already migrated to $action in this
release) build identically against an older SWIG that still recognizes it.

pypi.riseproject.dev hosts swig 4.3.1 for riscv64. An unbounded floor of
>=4.3.1 is not enough: PyPI itself now publishes a native riscv64 wheel
for swig 4.5.1 (swig-4.5.1-py3-none-manylinux_2_31_riscv64.whl), and
since CIBW_ENVIRONMENT only adds our registry via PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL
(PyPI stays the default index), pip picks the newest version satisfying
the constraint across both indexes -- 4.5.1, not our 4.3.1. SWIG 4.5
dropped the PyInt_*/PyString_* Python-2 compatibility macros that
outputPYTHON_wrap.c (SWIG-generated, not hand-written) still calls, so
the build fails with "implicit declaration of function 'PyInt_FromLong'".
An explicit upper bound keeps pip on the 4.3.1 we can actually supply.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 swmm-toolkit/pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/swmm-toolkit/pyproject.toml b/swmm-toolkit/pyproject.toml
index 564d84a..48c313b 100644
--- a/swmm-toolkit/pyproject.toml
+++ b/swmm-toolkit/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 [build-system]
-requires = ["swig>=4.4.0", "scikit-build-core>=0.4.3"]
+requires = ["swig>=4.3.1,<4.4.0", "scikit-build-core>=0.4.3"]
 build-backend = "scikit_build_core.build"

 [project]
